A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate when the **underlying cause matches** an open ticket.
[Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/) supersedes the old subject-only rule:

1. read the body and identify the tenant, its locale, form version and channel;
2. compare the cause with existing tickets, using the rendered views and source logic;
3. merge only with matching cause evidence; otherwise keep separate for investigation.

<Callout>
Equal subjects can hide different causes. Different subjects can report the same cause.
Browser locale and intake tags are not the tenant directory.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Do not merge uncertain reports on subject alone. See the
[signed review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review/) for the limits of the current classifier.
